  "final_text": "**None.** No file in the folder shows a restore test, so R7 is a **GAP**. The file you'd naturally send is `backup-report_2026-10.txt`, and it says the opposite:\n\n> \"Restore test: not done in 2026. Planned for Q4 2026 (owner: IT lead).\"\n\nR7 asks for \"a restore test of your backups from the last 12 months, with its result.\" Tannwald counts a document as current if it's dated on or after 10 December 2025.\n\n| File | Quote | QUOTE | PERIOD | SCOPE | APPROVAL | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `backup-report_2026-10.txt` (record) | \"Restore test: not done in 2026. Planned for Q4 2026\" | ✗ Shows the backup jobs ran, not a restore test; \"planned\" doesn't count | ✓ Generated 2026-11-01 | Servicepult export and file share | ✓ Generated by the backup system, owned by the IT lead | **GAP**: shows the test wasn't done |\n| `infosec-policy_v3_FINAL.md` (policy) | \"Backups are restore-tested twice a year.\" | ✗ A policy shows intent, and Tannwald asks for \"the record that shows it was done\" | ✗ Approved 2024-03-12; its review was due March 2025 | – | ✓ Managing Director | No evidence for R7 |\n| `it-notes_2026-10-06.md` (statement) | \"Backups are tested, the jobs run every night.\" | ✗ Personal notes; the backup report contradicts this | – | – | ✗ \"Not reviewed by anyone.\" | No evidence for R7 |\n\n**Don't send** the policy or the IT notes as R7 evidence. Tannwald would read the backup report next to them and see that what you claim doesn't match what you did. If you send the backup report, send it as what it is: proof the jobs ran, but no restore test.\n\nThe rule window also includes 10–31 December 2025. Whether a restore test happened then is not in the files. If one did, its record could close the gap.\n\n**What closes the gap:** a real restore test record before you send the documents on 25 November, or at the latest before the audit on 10 December. The report already plans a test for Q4 2026. The record should say which jobs were restored (Servicepult export, file share), when, how long it took, the result, and who ran it. Owner: IT lead.\n\n**Draft request to the IT lead:**\n> Tannwald's R7 asks for \"a restore test of your backups from the last 12 months, with its result,\" due 25 November. The October backup report says \"Restore test: not done in 2026,\" so we have no record. Was there a restore test between 10 and 31 December 2025? If so, please send its record. If not, can the Q4 test of the Servicepult export and file share run before 25 November, with a written result (date, what was restored, success or failure, time taken, who ran it)? \"No test exists\" is a perfectly good answer; we just need to know.\n\nWhether to tell Tannwald the test is still pending or run it first is your call.",
